  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilience Against Trafficking and Exploitation (CREATE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Climate Resilience Against Trafficking and Exploitation (CREATE) project is a pilot initiative focusing on the nexus between climate change and human trafficking. Working at the community-level in key hotspot locations in Ethiopia and Philippines, the project will seek to reduce risks of trafficking by supporting the communities to be more climate-resilient and trafficking-aware. The project will also contribute to enhancing the evidence-base on the ways in which climate change can impact migration and vulnerability to trafficking, and generate learning about potential responses.</narrative>
  </description>
